 "prompt": "The repository at /testbed has a bug, described below. Fix it by changing the source code; do not modify or\nadd tests. When you are done, the project's existing test suite should pass.\n\n<issue>\n_ContentTypeMap.__getitem__ raises NameError when partname not found\n\n#### Description\n\nWhen accessing a content type for a partname that doesn't exist in the content type map, a `NameError` is raised instead of the expected `KeyError`.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nfrom docx.opc.pkgreader import _ContentTypeMap\nfrom docx.opc.packuri import PackURI\n\nct_map = _ContentTypeMap()\n# This should raise KeyError but raises NameError instead\nct_map[PackURI('/!blat/rhumba.1x&')]\n```\n\nThe issue also affects the type checking behavior - when a non-PackURI key is used, it should raise a KeyError with a specific message about the wrong type, but instead raises a NameError.\n\n```python\nfrom docx.opc.pkgreader import _ContentTypeMap\nfrom docx.opc.packuri import PackURI\n\nct_map = _ContentTypeMap()\nct_map._overrides = {PackURI('/part/name1.xml'): 'app/vnd.type1'}\n# This should raise KeyError about wrong type but raises NameError instead  \nct_map['/part/name1.xml']\n```\n</issue>\n",
